.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2026/0/HF/5156/versions/0/","versions":[{"label":"Introduction","date":"2026-05-16","url":"https://www.revisor.mn.gov/bills/94/2026/0/HF/5156/versions/0/","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would set rules for certain prescription drugs that have a federal \"maximum fair price,\" which is the highest price set by the U.S. government. It would bar drug makers from charging more than that price in Minnesota and would require health plans and pharmacy benefit managers to pay at least that amount, or the national average drug acquisition cost if higher, plus dispensing fees. It would also limit drug makers from pulling these drugs from the state to avoid the price rules and set a penalty for doing so. The section would take effect January 1, 2027.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false}}}